# Diagram review cadence (ADR-2131) — TEMPLATE, rendered at boot.
#
# skills/sealmap-review/run-cron.sh reads [diagram_review] from the manifest, fills the
# @…@ placeholders below, writes the result under /run/agentbox (tmpfs, so nothing here ever
# outlives a boot or names a store path) and hands it to supercronic. Edit the schedules in
# agentbox.toml, not here.
#
# The PATH is the supervisor's ([program:diagram-review-cron] environment= in flake.nix); the
# API keys are inherited from the container environment. There is deliberately no PATH= line.
#
# Daily GLM triage: which topics did the day's code changes make wrong? Cheap, and it never
# edits a topic. With weekly_window = false the Gemini gate is also considered after it.
@GLM_TRIAGE_CRON@ node /home/devuser/workspace/project/agentbox/skills/sealmap-review/scripts/review-cadence.cjs triage 2>&1@TRIAGE_AUDIT@

# Nightly GLM review (critical and premortem lenses; unchanged shards are skipped by pack
# hash, so a quiet night is free), then the Gemini gate. The gate decides;
# a refusal is a ledger line, not an error. `;` not `&&`: a failed GLM review must not stop
# the gate from reading a high-severity finding GLM recorded earlier.
@GLM_REVIEW_CRON@ node /home/devuser/workspace/project/agentbox/skills/sealmap-review/scripts/review-cadence.cjs review-glm 2>&1 ; node /home/devuser/workspace/project/agentbox/skills/sealmap-review/scripts/review-cadence.cjs audit-gemini 2>&1
